branches=[
('WB07',[48],'Prior memo and unspecified edits','PARKMEMO is the earlier filled memo, although prose calls it a letter. The initial editing changes are not specified; a later bounded execution must declare them and its saved revision, not invent evidence.',['Q2','Q3']),
('WB07',[48,49],'Exit versus Cancel for settings','From the exit question, Yes exits,No clears andF1 keeps the document/caret; within margins, F7 commits whileF1 backs out without inserting a margin owner in this tested context. Source says most cases, not a universal cancel law.',['L1','Q1','Q2','Q3']),
('WB07',[49,50],'Native Undelete and history','The restored centered title includes its code; deletion of To/Date begins on Bold owners. Retain up to3 deletions, preview at current caret, cancel preview and restore at correct gaps. Up/Down are alternatives to PreviousDeletion cycling.',['E1','Q1','Q2','Q3']),
('WB07',[50],'Free Cancel experiment','The learner may experiment further, but no finite key sequence is supplied. Keep an unresolved optional exercise; do not fabricate a completed all-context Cancel corpus.',['Q1','Q2']),
('WB07',[50,51,52],'Help state transitions','Index letters, template, function-key reference topics and context-sensitive printer Help are distinct states. Topic keystrokes while in Help must not edit the document. Enter versus Space exits and repeatedF7 menu returns need exact focus/caret checks.',['P1','Q1','Q2','Q3']),
('WB07',[51],'Date/Time topic key','Step8 asks the learner to find the appropriate key rather than spelling it out. Preserve actual template/index mapping as a required source/interface witness; no guessed binding is added here.',['Q1','Q2']),
('WB07',[50,52],'Help files and disk swap','Two-drive setup needs WordPerfect1 disk inB for Help, then Learn disk restored. WPHELP.FIL has a registered fingerprint; this is not a current private availability or exact Help-content claim.',['O2','Q1','Q2']),
('WB07',[51,52],'Program identity and documentation correction','Capture real reference version/date and conditional registration data, not the1989 example header. WBC51 PDF2 correction573 qualifies the registration field; correction1636 removes the stray inch quote in margin step11.',['Q1','Q2']),
('WB07',[52,53],'Manual/tutorial and historical services','Reference sections/index, optional tutorial and historical support/publications are documentary context. Keep reproducibility/hardware-description advice; do not contact anyone, mail registration, assert current services or implement old institutions. Tutorial installation/execution remains unrun and is not expanded here.',['O2','Q1']),
('WB08',[54],'Teaching input and enter shorthand','MUSICBOX.WKB is the original rough draft; subsequent MUSICBOX is a distinct learner-saved output. Source defines enter as type then Enter. Preserve extension, source identity, working directory and selected printer.',['Q1','Q2','Q3']),
('WB08',[55,56,57,58],'Forward/backward deletion and screen scrolling','Delete removes at caret, Backspace before it; restore then remove word plus preceding space. Optional whole-letter scrolling must return to the prescribed paragraph. Source24visible rows/25th status is a declared display context, not a modern universal terminal size.',['E1','I4','Q1','Q2']),
('WB08',[58,59],'Word and hard-return boundaries','The phrase may be deleted characterwise as explanatory alternative; the numbered route deletes3 words. Ctrl-End removes line text but leaves HRt; subsequent Delete removes that owner. Preserve spacing, history and unrelated code boundaries.',['E1','Q1','Q2','Q3']),
('WB08',[60,61,62,63],'Automatic versus explicit page boundary','Declare8.5x11in/1in default margins and printer metrics. Status positions include margins. Added blank lines move text through a soft boundary; HardPage remains attached to its source gap. The source explicitly allows correcting a misplaced hard break via Backspace then reinsertion.',['E1','L1','L3','Q2','Q3']),
('WB08',[63,64],'Timed backup versus explicit Save','The1989 source describes30-minute backup, possible wait notice and removal on exit, while explicit Save preserves named work and continues editing. This is source evidence forS1/S2 follow-up, not modern autosave equivalence or observed March1992 behavior; later recovery section is referenced but not expanded here.',['S1','S2','Q3']),
('WB08',[64,65],'PageNumber placement and illustrated alternatives','Choose top-center every page and inspect the owner at the beginning before other text/codes; source warns late page-format placement begins on a later page. Other diagram positions/alternating-page choices/None are unselected source leads; no unseen coordinate mapping is guessed.',['L1','Q1','Q2','Q3']),
('WB08',[65,66],'Current-page suppression menu','SuppressPageNumber is this-page-only and leaves all-page numbering for following pages. Other pictured options include suppress all/headers/footers, bottom-center and individualHeader/FooterA/B; these remain unexecuted leads.',['L1','Q1','Q2','Q3']),
('WB08',[67],'Preview numbering and page geometry','Normal editing lacks printed page number; preview page1 suppression and page2 number are distinct. Source reserves two number/spacing lines.100percent/Home arrows pan the view, while doubleHome navigates document; do not conflate these states.',['L1','P3','I4','Q1','Q2']),
('WB08',[68,69],'Actual printer selection and persistence','Retrieving teaching input selects WorkbookPrinter; printing requires an actual installed printer. Save before print, choose own definition, inspect selection, and save that association for later retrieval. This requires real declared PRS/metrics and native/print evidence, not a metadata-only claim.',['L1','P1','Q2','Q3']),
('WB08',[69],'Optional Draft quality and printer menu','High is the example default; optional Draft may change speed/font depending on printer. Pictured Additional/Edit/Copy/Delete/Help/Update printer actions are unselected leads. No font/kerning command is introduced by this lesson.',['L1','P1','Q1','Q2']),
('WB09',[70,71],'Independent document screens','The source opens and switchesDoc1/Doc2 with independent document/caret/status. It does not invokeCtrlF3 Window or simultaneous split panes; no split-window evidence or implementation claim follows.',['I1','I4','Q2','Q3']),
('WB09',[71,72],'Memo filename/source discrepancy','Text says retrieveMEMO, prior learner form, while the picture showsMEMO.WKB. Both the prior form path and recorded teachingMEMO.WKB are distinct. Freeze exact intended artifact/profile in a later reviewed recipe; do not silently substitute or call a screenshot a native oracle.',['I1','L3','Q2','Q3']),
('WB09',[72,73,74],'Paragraph copy across documents','Retrieve the original rough MUSICBOX.WKB inDoc2, not the edited MUSICBOX output. Copy rather than cut preserves source; Paragraph selection includes two following hard returns that Sentence would omit. Retained paste payload survives switching and inserts at the prescribedDoc1 gap.',['I1','E3','Q1','Q2','Q3']),
('WB09',[74,75],'Block endpoints and physical mouse','Keyboard Block selection ends at first character of the following paragraph. Optional left-drag reaches the same intended list endpoint and BlockOn cue. Actual native range/physical host equivalence remains unrun.',['I1','I3','Q1','Q2','Q3']),
('WB09',[74,75],'Help and changed Block menu','Move on an active Block shows Block/column/rectangle choices rather than Sentence/Paragraph/Page/Retrieve. Selected ordinaryBlock is not a tabular/rectangular selection. Other variants remain unselected leads.',['Q1','Q2']),
('WB09',[75],'Menu Copy skips numbered steps','The EditCopy alternative at step5 jumps directly to step8, bypassing keyboard-route Help/Block/Copy steps6–7. Count all source numbers once but do not require both exclusive paths in one run. Copy turns Block off before switching.',['I1','Q1','Q2','Q3']),
('WB09',[76,77],'Repeat applied to command','Escape5/DeleteWord repeats a deletion command, not character entry or macro invocation. Source points toF3/Escape for the supported-feature list; that optional Help branch is unrun. Preserve exact5-word boundary and replacement text.',['E1','Q1','Q2']),
('WB09',[77],'Optional preview instead of print','Memo may be viewed before printing or instead of printing; these are explicit optional exercise outcomes with separate resources/evidence, not automatic print success.',['P3','P1','Q2']),
('WB09',[77,78],'ExitDoc2 versus clear versus Cancel','AfterNoSave, Yes closesDoc2 and returnsDoc1; No clearsDoc2 but keeps its screen; pictured Cancel returns to its document. Preserve Doc1 memo/dirty state and source disk bytes across each route. This is not the single-screen application-exit question.',['I1','Q2','Q3']),
('WB09',[78],'New memo save and later-source reference','SaveDoc1 under MUSBMEMO and decline application exit. Reference to later special techniques does not expand those methods in this census.',['I1','Q2','Q3']),
('WB07-WB09',[48,54,70],'Continuity and resource boundaries','Retain the earlier filled memo, original musicbox source, named edited letter and later new memo as distinct objects. Help/version files, teaching PRS, own printer, clock/display and two-drive adaptation are prerequisites, not inferred by green primitive tests.',['L1','O2','Q2','Q3'])]
